# A complete illegal-action chain, driven from inside somebody's bedroom.
#
#   dotnet run -- --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters \
#                 --start-at village --start-area bedroom --period noon --observe-only chest \
#                 --cli-timeout 240 --cli-script cli/crime.cli
#
# A private area makes EVERY verb a crime (the sealed setting test in Verb.IsIllegal), which is the
# only way a script reaches the crime machinery without hunting for a seed that puts a lockable door,
# a witness and an unscrupulous modus mentis in one room. --observe-only pins the phase to the chest,
# since a narration phase otherwise opens on whichever of four objects the persona picked.
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES: the observation -> think -> act -> dice -> outcome chain completes with every
# coded crime rule in the path, and nothing in it throws, hangs or blocks an action it should not.
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT PROVE, and what covers it instead — run `--crime-audit`:
#   * the willingness rules. --playground answers the persona-fit question without asking it, so the
#     filtered option set is never built;
#   * which rung of the consequence ladder fires. Both the acting modus mentis (a discreet one is not
#     heard through a wall at all) and the witness's whereabouts are drawn from the seed, so at
#     seed 42 this run gets away with it — correctly, via a discreet skill;
#   * the goal filters firing. They only narrow when the drawn thinking modus mentis is High or Low,
#     and in a private area where everything is a crime a Low one changes nothing.

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Inside a private room: everything the persona could want to do here is a crime.
state
expect-not IMPOSSIBLE
advance 12 180
regions

# The keyword opens thinking. The goal choice runs here, behind the choice rules.
click keyword chest
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
state
regions

# Execute it. fail-dice forces the roll to fail, which is what hands a witness in earshot the
# caught-red-handed confrontation — when one is in earshot and the skill was not discreet.
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
state
quit
